WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.410
"The New Colossus"

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.540
by Emma Lazarus

00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:12.209
Not like the brazen giant of Greek fame,

00:00:12.209 --> 00:00:17.299
With conquering limbs astride 
from land to land;

00:00:17.299 --> 00:00:22.268
Here at our sea-washed, 
sunset gates shall stand

00:00:22.268 --> 00:00:26.568
A mighty woman with a torch, whose flame

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:31.098
Is the imprisoned lightning, and her name

00:00:31.098 --> 00:00:35.698
Mother of Exiles. From her beacon-hand

00:00:35.698 --> 00:00:40.678
Glows world-wide welcome; 
her mild eyes command

00:00:40.678 --> 00:00:45.298
The air-bridged harbor 
that twin cities frame.

00:00:45.298 --> 00:00:49.868
“Keep, ancient lands, your 
storied pomp!” cries she

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:56.118
With silent lips. “Give me your tired, 
your poor,

00:00:56.118 --> 00:00:59.898
Your huddled masses yearning 
to breathe free,

00:00:59.898 --> 00:01:03.738
The wretched refuse of your teeming shore.

00:01:03.738 --> 00:01:08.398
Send these, the homeless, 
tempest-tost to me,

00:01:08.398 --> 00:01:12.389
I lift my lamp beside the golden door!”

